    "main_topic": [
      {
        "h_title": "About Phuket Airport (HKT)",
        "main_title": "Phuket Airport (HKT)",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Phuket Airport (HKT) is a major international airport and is one of the busiest in Thailand, after Bangkok! The airport is located about 30 kilometres from Phuket Town, close to Mai Khao Beach, where plane spotting has become a popular pastime. Phuket Airport has three terminals, with Terminal 1 being used for international flights, Terminal 2 for domestic and Terminal X reserved for charter flights and to handle overflow.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Check-in",
        "main_title": "Phuket Airport (HKT)",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "There are three terminals at Phuket Airport: Terminal 1 (international), Terminal 2 (domestic) and Terminal X. It’s always a good idea to arrive at the airport nice and early for your flight, and to confirm check-in times and locations directly with your airline as each may have different requirements. It’s often possible to check in for your flights online in advance via your airline’s website or app, which can be an easy way to save time at the airport on the day of travel.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Baggage",
        "main_title": "Phuket Airport (HKT)",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Baggage allowances vary by airline and ticket class, so it’s important to confirm what’s included with your flight booking to avoid any surprises at bag drop. For more specific information on baggage limits, such as the size, weight and number of bags included in your airfare, check with your airline or ask your Travel Expert for assistance. Travellers flying through Phuket Airport can make use of the self-serve bag drop kiosks within the Domestic and International Departure Halls.",
            "url": "http://www.flightcentre.com.au/stores",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "http://www.flightcentre.com.au/stores",
                "anchor_text": "ask your Travel Expert"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Facilities",
        "main_title": "Phuket Airport (HKT)",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "There are a wide range of facilities available at Phuket Airport for your comfort, convenience and use before or after your flight.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Baggage storage, luggage wrapping and trolleys",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
